  message: "DONE — status correction, not new work. This item's own 2026-07-20 discussion entry opens \"KEYSTONE LANDED (2026-07-19, PR merged f56ca6a23c)\" while its status stayed todo_soft, so `tracker ready` has been surfacing it as actionable ever since.\n\nIts titled deliverable IS shipped: [tool.mypy] is strict + the 11 pyright-resonant enable_error_code entries + namespace_packages, and scripts/check-mypy-ratchet runs one whole-tree invocation against a shrink-only per-error-code baseline (.ci/mypy-strict-baseline.json), with the CI job rewritten off the per-package loop.\n\nThe residual its note names — \"the drain to zero (this item's 'ratchet each package to zero (the L bulk)')\" — is verbatim INV-zogud's statement (\"running mypy <repo> with the strict config from a clean tree must produce zero errors\"). Keeping this item open therefore duplicates INV-zogud rather than tracking anything INV-zogud does not, and the ordered remainder already has owners: the drain is INV-zogud, the blocking flip is WI-rabum (--mode=strict), the type:ignore audit is WI-gapig (already this item's isbefore).\n\nRe-homed rather than re-scoped, so the ready queue stops offering a landed keystone as available work."  # e589
